description: 'Replace the string prefix_module model with first-class path-scoped
  package identity (docs/lamp-prereqs.md §1). PackageId{name, owner_scope, version,
  semantic_hash} threaded through resolve -> HIR -> MIR -> codegen mangling. Path-scoped
  resolution (use bar in baz -> foo:baz:bar; local, no global arbitration). Symbol
  mangling <pkgid-hash>_<module>_<name> replacing flat module_name. Reexport consent
  (use baz/bar legal only when baz declares reexport bar; reach-in = hard error).
  Multi-version coexistence (use foo@1 as foo1 / use foo@2 as foo2 -> distinct non-unifiable
  identities, separate cap unions). Workspace flattening (members -> one DAG, collisions
  hard error). Retire prefix_module; keep single-package fast path assigning root
  PackageId. Decide PackageId home (lean: interned handle + side table). Blocked by
  2-32-1 (Q4 multi-version/coherence decision). Definition of done: scoped identity
  end-to-end with tests for path resolution, reexport consent, and (deferred-or-implemented
  per Q4) multi-version.'
